  "source_text": "Synthetic validation nurse note. No real patient data.\n\nThe driver has established diabetes. The current specialist letter confirms that diabetes is managed with insulin and that the diabetes is not gestational. The driver has been adjusting meal times around split shifts and sometimes receives a sensor warning before feeling symptoms, but there is no documented recent episode requiring another person's assistance and no complete assessment of hypoglycaemia awareness in the material provided.\n\nThe ophthalmologist confirms non-physiological diplopia following a recent examination. Diplopia is present within 20 degrees of central fixation. The driver says the double image is more noticeable after prolonged night driving, yet the specialist reproduced it during daytime testing, so its absence during a short nursing interview is not treated as proof that the documented finding has resolved.\n\nA change of lenses has been proposed but not assessed, and the nurse has no updated specialist decision about the visual symptoms or the diabetes monitoring plan. The two confirmed findings are recorded independently; neither a successful lens adjustment nor adequate glucose control has been assumed.\n",
